{"kind":"assert","text":"Rulings on `5557247a`, the joint EK-1 and ES-1 draft.\n\nAccepted: one function export from `packages/derive`,\n`judgeExploreGrant`, and no type export. Accepted: one\nsession-ending reason, `refused` with `unauthorized`, pinned in\n`session.test.ts`. I tell the owner that the exception adds one\nfunction.\n\n1. Opt-in, as the joint draft has it. A caller passes\n   `standing: true`, and only the MCP server and the command line\n   do. The application gateway stays closed to a query on a POST\n   to `sessions`. No screen page reads the standing before step\n   E2. E2 opens the gateway for `standing`, with its test and its\n   row in `entry-points.md`. I add that line to the E2 request.\n2. Read `kind` from the member item, in the read that the\n   inventory keeps for the handle. `kind` is a fixed field of the\n   record. It decides no action, so the one judge of eligibility\n   stays. `#keepsOriginals` keeps its exclusion. Add no read for\n   it. If the member item is not held, `kind` is absent, as today.\n3. Yes. Seal the changed sources again at apply with the\n   repository's tool. The review text lists each sealed file that\n   changed, with one line on the reason, so that the Security\n   conclusion reads those diffs.\n\nApply after AE-1 lands. The gate order stands: AE-1, then C4, then\nthis head.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}